      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because we\u0027re allowing PD communication during RO (we don\u0027t actually have anyway to disable PD communication with PDCs), what about creating a new `SYS_INIT()` hook specifically for enabling EFS2 when PDCs are present.\n\nLooking at `vboot_main()`, I think we only need to check if we\u0027re in RO and then call `verify_and_jump()`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "6935b6a787556ef8d34a29822b1aeb55df8ad484",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e922a218_2daf5079",
        "filename": "zephyr/app/ec/ec_app_main.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 99,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T21:20:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The PDC drivers and PDC subsystem aren\u0027t initialized until `POST_KERNEL` at priorities 90 and 91 respectively.\n\nEFS2 should only depend on the UART and GPIO drivers (since we don\u0027t need to check for recovery mode).  These both have defaulr priorities of 50 - `CONFIG_SERIAL_INIT_PRIORITY` and `CONFIG_GPIO_INIT_PRIORITY`.",
      "parentUuid": "b019492f_b6b2e793",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "6935b6a787556ef8d34a29822b1aeb55df8ad484",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
